    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "piechart",
      "title": "Fraud decision mix",
      "description": "The in-path verdict mix as the SEND FLOW saw it \u2014 which is why it includes the two verdicts only the caller can observe. SKIPPED is capacity: the 200ms budget was blown and the send proceeded unscored (ADR-0005). FRAUD_ERROR is correctness: the check was BROKEN \u2014 a 401/403, a drifted contract, a bug \u2014 so the send also proceeded unscored, but this one will not fix itself when load falls (ADR-0018). Both are risk, not drop-off; neither ever reaches the wire.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "platinumcoin-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "right",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "pieType": "donut",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNonNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "platinumcoin-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (decision) (pix_fraud_decision_total)",
          "legendFormat": "{{decision}}",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Fail-open rate vs 5% ceiling",
      "description": "How often the 200ms fraud budget was blown and the send proceeded UNSCORED \u2014 CAPACITY fail-opens only, since ADR-0018 moved broken checks onto their own FRAUD_ERROR series and the fraud_broken alert. Fail-open is a deliberate design (availability of payments over completeness of scoring); this number is what keeps it a documented exception rather than the norm.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "platinumcoin-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 5
